      "id": "PKri",
      "code_hash": "74abf5dfc998bffa34fa5ed9f69e8925",
      "outputs": [
        {
          "type": "data",
          "data": {
            "text/markdown": "<span class=\"markdown prose dark:prose-invert contents\"><h1 id=\"d1-api-use-case\">D1 API use case</h1>\n<span class=\"paragraph\">In this notebook, we will show a simple use case involving interactions with D1 associated to a\nCloudflare account. This will involve the following:<br></span>\n<span class=\"paragraph\">1. listing existing D1 datasets;<br></span>\n<span class=\"paragraph\">2. simple query fetching rows from a D1 dataset table;<br></span>\n<span class=\"paragraph\">all using the Cloudflare API.</span>\n<span class=\"paragraph\"><strong>Prerequisites:</strong><br></span>\n<span class=\"paragraph\">- API token (see <a href=\"https://developers.cloudflare.com/fundamentals/api/get-started/create-token/\" rel=\"noopener\" target=\"_blank\">here</a>\nfor info on how to create one) with <strong>D1 read</strong> permission;<br></span>\n<span class=\"paragraph\">- at least one D1 dataset with a table.</span></span>"
          }
        }
      ],
      "console": []
    },
    {
      "id": "SFPL",
      "code_hash": "d1891dac497223a4d916d675398e37ab",
      "outputs": [
        {
          "type": "data",
          "data": {
            "text/markdown": "<span class=\"markdown prose dark:prose-invert contents\"><h2 id=\"list-available-d1-datasets\">List available D1 datasets</h2>\n<span class=\"paragraph\">By performing a GET request (with no payload) to the <code>/accounts/{account_id}/d1/database</code>\n<a href=\"https://developers.cloudflare.com/api/resources/d1/subresources/database/methods/list/\" rel=\"noopener\" target=\"_blank\">endpoint</a>\nwe can get the names, unique Ids as well as other info of all D1 datasets associated with a Cloudflare account.</span></span>"
          }
        }
      ],
      "console": []
    },
    {
      "id": "Kclp",
      "code_hash": "c81282a82384af46731b34f7729507b6",
      "outputs": [
        {
          "type": "data",
          "data": {
            "text/markdown": "<span class=\"markdown prose dark:prose-invert contents\"><div class=\"admonition\">\n<span class=\"paragraph\">The same endpoint can also be used for creating a new D1 dataset. This can be done by performing a POST\nrequest with the name of the dataset as the payload.</span>\n</div></span>"
          }
        }
      ],
      "console": []
    },
    {
      "id": "emfo",
      "code_hash": "7cb5dfa8687bc9a562ba594f9b770fa8",
      "outputs": [
        {
          "type": "data",
          "data": {
            "text/markdown": "<span class=\"markdown prose dark:prose-invert contents\"><h2 id=\"performing-queries\">Performing queries</h2>\n<span class=\"paragraph\">Queries to D1 databases using the API are made using POST requests to\n<code>/accounts/{account_id}/d1/database/{database_id}/query</code>\n<a href=\"https://developers.cloudflare.com/api/resources/d1/subresources/database/methods/query/\" rel=\"noopener\" target=\"_blank\">endpoint</a>.\nThe query (as well as optional query parameters) must be added as payload.</span></span>"
          }
        }
      ],
      "console": []
    },
    {
      "id": "nWHF",
      "code_hash": "7f857795ed39bacfcc42ec383c58d7fc",
      "outputs": [
        {
          "type": "data",
          "data": {
            "text/markdown": "<span class=\"markdown prose dark:prose-invert contents\"><div class=\"admonition\">\n<p class=\"admonition-title\">Setting up D1 datasets</span>\n<span class=\"paragraph\">While not shown in this notebook, SQL tables can be created and populated on the API side by running queries\nwith <code>CREATE TABLE</code> and <code>INSERT INTO</code> respectively. Both of these will require tokens with <code>write</code>\npermissions, however, and represent a more manual approach to populating SQL tables. The alternative would be\nto import an already existing database into D1.</span>\n<span class=\"paragraph\">More information on how to import (and export) data from D1 datasets can be found in\n<a href=\"https://developers.cloudflare.com/d1/best-practices/import-export-data/\" rel=\"noopener\" target=\"_blank\">this dev page</a>.</span>\n</div>\n<span class=\"paragraph\">Queries vary from table to table, so we will perform a simple fetch of the first 10 lines of a given table.</span></span>"
          }
        }
      ],
      "console": []
    },
